Project Goal

Mobile-first load: reduce initial HTML size + DOM weight

Single source of truth: no more copy/paste sections

OOP-ish patterns in JS: build repeatable UI blocks

Offline durability stays: worker + snapshot + restore unchanged

Progressive enhancement stays: details/summary works without JS

Success Criteria (definition of “done”)

Initial HTML becomes a shell (header + mount point + template tags if needed)

Checklist renders from data config + component classes

Same visual output as today (styling preserved)

Worker snapshot still restores state after reload

Mic buttons still appear on text fields

Performance: faster first render on phone (less HTML download + fewer DOM nodes at startup)

Architecture Options (choose 1, I recommend #2)
Option 1 — Pure OOP classes that generate HTML strings

Fast to write, compact

Harder to diff test, can get “stringy”

✅ Option 2 — “Component factory” + small classes (recommended)

Each component has:

render() returns DOM node (not string)

bind() attaches events

Easy to test, less fragile

Option 3 — Templates + data (template tags)

Use <template> elements + clone

Very clean and fast, still “component-like”

Less “OOP vibe” but better for maintainability

